1. `search_a` can be very large (all coprime values up to ell)
2. `valid_A_y` and `valid_B_x` grow large with many gap patterns
3. `search_d` iterates over all coprime values up to m
4. The cross product of all these is enormous

I need to dramatically reduce candidate count while keeping the high-quality patterns. Let me add hard caps and be more selective.

